@startuml native-interop
!pragma layout smetana
title M6 shared native worker, callback context and ownership
interface IInspector
class NativeInspector {
  InspectAsync(job, samples, token)
  DisposeAsync() / Dispose()
}
class Operation {
  copied managed input
  GCHandle context
  token registration
}
class NativeInspectorHandle {
  SafeHandle / ReleaseHandle()
}
interface INativeInspectionApi {
  PInvokeInspectionApi or CliNativeApi
  Start / RequestStop / Wait
}
class "inspection_handle (C++)" as NativeObject {
  copied vector
  worker thread
  atomic stop flag
}
NativeInspector ..|> IInspector
NativeInspector *-- NativeInspectorHandle : owns
NativeInspector *-- Operation : at most one active
Operation --> INativeInspectionApi : Start / RequestStop / Wait
Operation --> NativeInspectorHandle : extra reference until confirmed join
NativeInspectorHandle ..> NativeObject : Destroy through selected release function
INativeInspectionApi ..> NativeObject : C ABI v2
NativeObject ..> Operation : static callback / rooted context
note right of Operation
Start copies pinned input before returning.
Wait joins the worker and all callbacks.
Then unregister token, free context and release extra reference.
Late progress after stop is suppressed; in-flight callback must return.
end note
note bottom of NativeInspector
Host awaits Engine disposal, then adapter disposal.
Stop failure: join, fault engine, release safely.
Wait failure: retain handle reference + GCHandle until process exit.
Faulted engine rejects all new runs.
end note
@enduml
